cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use DL-VizLab or the Neural Program Model in your work, please cite it as below.'
title: 'DL-VizLab: an observable, replayable deep-learning training environment built on the Neural Program Model'
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-13
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/2GOVINDHR2/viz'
# Replace with the full author list before the release is archived on Zenodo.
authors:
  - name: 'The DL-VizLab authors'
keywords:
  - deep learning
  - education
  - visualization
  - intermediate representation
  - backpropagation
abstract: >-
  A browser-only learning environment in which every operation of neural-network
  training is recorded as an instruction of the Neural Program Model (NPM), a
  formally specified, serializable and replayable intermediate representation.
  Learners step through a run at six granularities, forwards and backwards, with
  each step explained by its general formula, the same formula with the step's
  numbers, and a sentence. Includes a curriculum of ten experiments, a CNN on
  reduced MNIST, a study mode that runs a three-condition evaluation, and an
  analysis pipeline validated on simulated data.
